# ---- Vendored browser libraries (static/vendor) ----
# Unlike the runtimes above, these are committed to the repo and embedded in
# the binary, so this is a tamper check on what ships rather than a gate on a
# download: `make vendor` (run by `make check`) re-verifies each committed file
# in place against the hash below, and re-fetches only one that has gone
# missing. DOMPurify is the load-bearing one — it is the only thing between a
# decrypted note and the page holding every key — so it is pinned like the rest.
# Each file is byte-for-byte the upstream named in its comment, except
# katex.min.css, which is that release trimmed to the woff2 faces this repo
# vendors (the upstream woff/ttf fallback src lists are removed). To move a
# version: bump it in the Makefile, re-fetch, re-trim the CSS if needed, and
# record the new hash here deliberately.

